  "id": "lipreading",
  "term": "lipreading",
  "definition": "Lipreading is understanding spoken speech by using visible mouth movements and other visual speech cues, especially when sound is limited or hard to hear. In this study context, it was measured as visual-only speech perception and related to people’s own ratings of their lipreading ability.",
